ck shift and swath are correct and checked against STK, and you identify the swath-versus-resolution trade-off well. To make progress conclusive, add a computed revisit or repeat-cycle time to back your weekly-coverage conclusion, include STK outputs such as ground tracks or coverage plots, and complete the launch analysis required by R2.\",\"C4\":\"Your report has a clear headed structure, consistent IEEE-style citations in order of appearance, and labelled figures and tables, which makes it easy to follow. To polish it, rephrase awkward sentences such as 'not even the full extent of their nurture', add the missing authors and dates for references [4], [8] and [9], and consider replacing the weaker source [11] with a more authoritative one.\"}}",
